# 0003. Startup is silent and fast: no process per shell, tool inits cached

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

A new shell reaches a usable prompt in ~50 ms, prints nothing and starts no process that
could be cached.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: `eval "$(tool init zsh)"` and generated completions start a process on every
  shell (~10 ms each), compinit re-scans fpath every time, and any output before the prompt
  breaks p10k's instant prompt.
- **Budget**: ~50 ms to a usable prompt (now ~60 ms), measured with `make bench` (10
  interactive startups via `$EPOCHREALTIME`). `make check` runs `zsh -i` under `script` and
  fails if startup prints anything; it can flake once without a real terminal.
- **`_cached_source <name> <cmd...>`** (`conf.d/40-tools.zsh`): skips if the tool is missing;
  writes the init to `$ZSH_CACHE_DIR/<name>.zsh`, `zcompile`s it, and regenerates only when
  the tool's binary is newer than the cache (`$commands[x] -nt $cache`). Used for zoxide,
  fzf (`fzf --zsh`), atuin (`--disable-up-arrow`, after fzf so its Ctrl-R wins), direnv and
  mise.
- **`_cached_completion <cmd> <cmd...>`**: writes `_<cmd>` into
  `$ZSH_CACHE_DIR/completions` (first in fpath) in the background (`&!`, via a `.tmp` file
  then `mv`). Used for kubectl, helm, gh, uv, k9s, kind; terraform uses `bashcompinit` +
  `complete -C`.
- **compinit** (`conf.d/30-completion.zsh`): full `compinit -i` and a background `zcompile`
  only when the dump is missing or older than 24 h (`(#qN.mh+24)`), otherwise `compinit -C`.
- **No process where a value can be computed**: `GOPATH` defaults to `~/go` instead of
  `$(go env GOPATH)`; atuin's session id is a UUIDv7 built in zsh from `$EPOCHREALTIME` and
  `$RANDOM` (`printf -v ATUIN_SESSION ...`) instead of `atuin uuid`, regenerated per `SHLVL`.
- **PATH**: `typeset -gU path fpath` keeps entries unique; `(N-/)` drops missing dirs.
- **No network at startup** (except the one-time zinit clone).
- **Consequences**: fast, quiet startup with instant prompt. Stale caches: after changing how
  a tool is initialised, `make clean`; new completions appear the next day or after
  `make clean`; the first shell after installing a tool lacks its completion. The atuin
  block must follow atuin's UUID format if it changes.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: zsh `zcompile`, `zsh/datetime`, compinit; zoxide, fzf, atuin, direnv, mise.
- Alternatives: plain `eval "$(tool init zsh)"`: ~10 ms per tool per shell;
  evalcache-style plugins: a dependency for a 10-line function.
